From 62ab197b584ada56c0e12737e1d8db421b1fab8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sbihaiko <bihaiko@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:12:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: one command and one barrier pair for a run of
 in-order uploads, with EDEN_NX2_UPLOAD_BATCH=1

BufferCacheRuntime::CopyBuffer records an upload that cannot go to the
upload command buffer as its own command, with a full barrier before the
copy and one after. Lichii counted 614 such copies and 1,212 barriers a
frame in Ocarina of Time, nearly all ~200-byte inline writes into GPU-written
pages, in runs outside render passes. With the switch, stream buffer uploads
join an UploadBatch (upload_batch.h): copies with the same source and
destination share one vkCmdCopyBuffer, and the batch never holds two copies
that write the same bytes or one that writes a buffer another reads (such a
copy, or a 65th, records the batch first). Any other recorded command, the
worker handoff and the submission record a pending batch first, so it stays
in order and in the tick that protects its staging regions. Dedicated
staging buffers keep the old path. The barrier after a copy, and
PostCopyBarrier's, also reach transfers with the switch: a reordered upload
of the same bytes in a later submission has no barrier of its own before it
(a synchronization fix Lichii found under the validation layer).

FPS unmeasured upstream; the gain is fewer recorded commands and barriers.
Off by default; with the switch unset the recorded commands are unchanged.
Port of Lichii #1245.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
